nt and ataxic presentation", "Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA): glucose is normal and lacks metabolic acidosis (HCO3- 22 mEq/L)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional features (weight loss, fever, night sweats)", "Suspicious blast count in peripheral blood"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Without evidence of infection or inflammation, reactive leukocytosis (B5) is unlikely, further supporting myeloid neoplasm (B1)."], "evidence_against": ["Absence of bone pain and normal creatinine slightly reduces likelihood of myeloid neoplasm (B1) but does not exclude it, as these features are not always prese…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 1.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.19140624999999997, "posterior": 0.36697651145498195, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Absence of bone pain and normal creatinine slightly reduces likelihood of myeloid neoplasm (B1) but does not exclude it, as these features are not always prese…"], "evidence_against": ["Older age at presentation with high blast count is more typical of myeloid leukemia (AML/CML-BC) than lymphoid leukemia (ALL), moderately weakening B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_re